{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch","id":899437,"title":"Which Splats Are The Best For Playing An \u00dcbermensch?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-25T15:04:30-07:00","id":899437,"title":"Which Splats Are The Best For Playing An \u00dcbermensch?","content":"I'd say Demon, Beast and Mage. I'm not an expert on Nietzsche, so take this with a spoon of salt.<br /> <br /> Demons can have just about any characteristic as a Virtue or Vice. With the &quot;Living The Lie&quot; Merit, they can gain Willpower from the Virtues and Vices of all their Covers, not just the main one. The Agendas, Catalysts and espionage-centered gameplay encourage a very individualistic mindset. The existence of Antinomians shows that it's possible for Demons to not act solely based on the leftovers of their angelic programming. Even those who stick closer to their original function can learn, adapt and explore much more freely than Angels.<br /> <br /> Beasts do not have Breaking Points in the way other splats have. Their grim necessities can often lead to an inner turmoil, but those who embrace their heritage can defy the notion that they are just forces of destruction meant to die by the sword. However, this notion is often introduced to them by other Beasts, and the way some of them teach might be too dogmatic and invasive for an \u00dcbermensch. It seems that the Incarnates are the true Over-Beasts, as they are not bound to the rules of Heroes or even other monsters.<br /> <br /> The shared vocabulary of Mages and the four main Orders speaks for itself: Sleepers, Lie, Awakened, the list goes on. They are practically synonymous with the Will To Power (one of their alternate names is even &quot;Will-Workers&quot;). Though the Orders have different approaches to Wisdom, it favors carefulness and subtlety over any Sleeper notion of fairness or mercy. The Seers might be an edge case: they have no qualms about ignoring all the rules of mere mortals and stepping on them, but the will of their Exarchs always comes first.<br /> <br /> An honorable mention goes to Hunters and the Code they create for themselves in order to better uphold the Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:34:28-07:00","id":899528,"title":"","content":"Well a Changeling at 10 wyrd is, when Embracing the Wyrd, potentially literally good at everything.<br /> <br /> I mean +10 per turn bonus dice, for anything invovling defence, resistance stats, or instant or extended actions, which means basically everything except reflex actions (unless said action involves resistance).<br /> <br /> On top of that the Wyrd 10 Changeling can unleash bedlam, turning an area the size of a foot ball field into a riot, orgy, and terrorified people fleeing, once per scene, plus a bunch of other stuff.<br /> <br /> Oh and Changeling is effectively immortal, without undeath or relying upon mage spells.<br /> <br /> And so much more, like if after scouring the mask, the Changeling with 10 wyrd hits someone with a damage contract, the Changeling deals no less then 10 damage.<br /> <br /> Or on other sorts of contracts gets an automatic exceptional success (well a 1 wyrd changeling can do that part).<br /> <br /> If said Chamgeling has 10 Clarity as well it gets more interesting still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:56:42-07:00","id":899550,"title":"","content":"Disregarding the problems of the subject matter, the answer is &quot;None of them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because none of them are human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:07:52-07:00","id":899563,"title":"","content":"Be mindful that &quot;ubermensch&quot; has largely grown beyond its philosophical origins and isnow most commonly associated with Nazi ideology, with the companion &quot;untermensch&quot; referring to all the non-Aryan races they wish to exterminate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]