iew Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't mages technically human, tho?</div> </div> </div> </div>*giggles* That's the question, idn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T19:23:14-07:00","id":899655,"title":"","content":"Physically, yes, but by giving them Wisdom in place of human Integrity the game says that because they have seen through the Lie they no longer share the human viewpoint or experience. Virtue and Vice for a Mage is not the same as it is for humans. All summed up in the idea that to a Mage calculated murder is somehow more innocent then a crime of passion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T20:27:21-07:00","id":899694,"title":"","content":"None of them.<br /> All the splats have to follow some sort of code of conduct/morality that prevents them from being true \u00dcbermensch.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T22:33:19-07:00","id":899759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899694#post899694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of them.<br /> All the splats have to follow some sort of code of conduct/morality that prevents them from being true \u00dcbermensch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the Ubermensch is the Ubermensch by having their values transcend themselves and become broader principles that guide the rest of the species, this seems wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T22:40:06-07:00","id":899767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899759#post899759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that the Ubermensch is the Ubermensch by having their values transcend themselves and become broader principles that guide the rest of the species, this seems wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just makes me imagine an elder carthian vampire.... Imposing his eldritch laws upon all of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T22:44:46-07:00","id":899771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899767#post899767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just makes me imagine an elder carthian vampire.... Imposing his eldritch laws upon all of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd play in that campaign.<br /> <br /> It'd be kind of awesome to see the Carthians completely split on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T23:26:17-07:00","id":899798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899759#post899759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that the Ubermensch is the Ubermensch by having their values transcend themselves and become broader principles that guide the rest of the species, this seems wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what \u00fcbermensch are. \u00fcbermensch are people who follow only their own code, who create their own value, uninfluenced by anyone or anything else. He isn't a creator of values for others to follow. He isn't a master imposing his will upon others.<br /> <br /> Vampires can't be \u00fcbermensch, they cling to humanities value, they are the very opposite of \u00fcbermensch.<br /> Werewolves can't be \u00dcbermensch, they are beholden to rules and laws of spirits and Luna.<br /> Mages cannot be \u00fcbermensch, their wisdom, their very magic show the idea of the \u00dcbermensch to be wrong, there are rules and values external they must follow or fight against.<br /> Demons can't be \u00fcbermensch, they know god exist, they define their entire existence by their opposition to god. They do not make their own values. Maybe reaching hell would make them \u00fcbermensch but they aren't yet.<br /> Beast cannot be \u00fcbermensch, they are slave to a parasitic astral monster.<br /> Promethean cannot be \u00dcbermensch, they seek to join the throng of humanity instead of freeing themselves from it. They are no different than vampires in that reguard.<br /> Changelings cannot be \u00fcbermensch. Their entire existence lies upon making pacts and stories, using these tools to impose rules and obey said rules on the universe and others. An \u00fcbermensch would follow his own rules.<br /> Mummies cannto be \u00fcbermensch, they are beholden to ancient contracts and purpose that is not truly their own.<br /> Sin eater cannot be Ubermensch, they too follow the rules of a symbiotic entity much like beasts do.<br /> Hunters could be \u00dcbermensch, in fact, they are the closest to the \u00fcbermensch, hunters make their own rules, set their own purpose. As long as they do not join a conspiracy, then they stop being \u00fcbermensch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T23:52:38-07:00","id":899804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899798#post899798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what \u00fcbermensch are. \u00fcbermensch are people who follow only their own code, who create their own value, uninfluenced by anyone or anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>This definition makes it functionally impossible for an \u00fcbermensch to actually exist within the Chronicles of Darkness as more than a myth, given that the extent to which things are connected is quite extensive and explicit and your criteria appear to include literally not having any connection to anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T01:09:55-07:00","id":899846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899804#post899804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This definition makes it functionally impossible for an \u00fcbermensch to actually exist within the Chronicles of Darkness as more than a myth, given that the extent to which things are connected is quite extensive and explicit and your criteria appear to include literally not having any connection to anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not my criteria, it's the criteria laid out Nietzsche. And it's not about not having connections to anything, it's about only following your own moral code and rules. Not having your will subordinate to anything or anyone else. It's about being yourself without needing to belong to anything else.<br /> <br /> The \u00fcbermensch is impossible in the world of darkness not because there are connection but because there are gods, there are moral/ethical principles derived from on high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T01:18:54-07:00","id":899850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899798#post899798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast cannot be \u00fcbermensch, they are slave to a parasitic astral monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they aren't. Often that astral monster, is themselves. It's like complaining you're a slave to your digestive system... <br /> <br /> Also, they definitely are not slaves when they become incarnate. No morality or code beyond the one they give themselves, above even the weaknesses their kind is meant to possess, above even the narrative they are meant to be part of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-26-2016, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T01:25:16-07:00","id":899853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899846#post899846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The \u00fcbermensch is impossible in the world of darkness not because there are connection but because there are gods, there are moral/ethical principles derived from on high.</div> </div> </div> </div>Half the &quot;gods&quot; you're referring to are massive collections of interconnected occult principles* whose aggregate input is more or less confined to existing as forces that act upon themselves and the mundane world.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* Or parts of those collections or third parties exploiting those connections or similar secondhand associates. Most gods are not strictly speaking free-willed beings.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-26-2016, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T01:57:31-07:00","id":899869,"title":"","content":"Isn't the Sage concept of the Silver Ladder basically an \u00dcbermensch? One chapter of their Order book even starts with a Nietzsche's quote about man being a bridge between an animal and the Overman.<br /> <br /> Mages have Virtues and Vices like typical humans. Wisdom is about knowing more things than the average human and acting accordingly, not an inherently alien way of thinking. Unlike vampires with their Frenzy, or the Blood Rage of werewolves, both of which are largely independent on their bearers' respective wills, mages don't have <i>alien</i> desires, and they have to consciously decide to and work on maintaining their wisdom and perspective, often <i>despite</i> their inner all too human passions (when you remove your vice with the Amorality spell, you can't even cause acts of Hubris). Mages might be monsters, but they are certainly human.<br /> <br /> Their inner drive to know more has literally created their first Obsession, having obsessions is simply who they are and who they were as a mortal, they wouldn't have Awakened otherwise. And while many of them fall, the ideal of being a mage is to *become* an idea so powerful that it remakes them into a symbol of certain values, values they have because of what they are, not because of what they were told to be. To be given orders, and as a result of obeying them eventually Ascending is what the Seers are about. The Pentacle as a whole, especially Silver Ladder, is practically the \u00dcbermensch personified, individual cases notwithstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 05-26-2016, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T03:47:02-07:00","id":899905,"title":"","content":"Hieromagus. Nuff said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T04:59:24-07:00","id":899929,"title":"","content":"*Shrugs* The ubermensch is idea of evolution of humans though artificial selection. This is pretty much the wheelhouse of the God Machine. So, from that perspective, I'm going to say that Fractals are the ubermensch. Go demon-children!<br /> <br /> Mages also have a strong ubermensch-vibe. As in, transcending the human condition to become something more is pretty much a major point of the game, and kind of the idea behind the Ubermensch. The idea of the Ubermensch also posits that the idea of God is meaningless and holds no value in current society - from a Mage perspective, that means that the Exarchs and serving them is bad. Which, it is. Wisdom isn't a code of conduct given from on high - its a personal understanding how to use your magic without it spiraling out of control. <br /> <br /> However, where I veer away from mages is the idea that the ubermensch is the result of genetic manipulation across generations, while mage is more about using magic to artificially evolve individuals. Genetics plays no part in mage transcendance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-26-2016, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:49:31-07:00","id":899990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899929#post899929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Shrugs* The ubermensch is idea of evolution of humans though artificial selection. This is pretty much the wheelhouse of the God Machine. So, from that perspective, I'm going to say that Fractals are the ubermensch. Go demon-children!<br /> <br /> Mages also have a strong ubermensch-vibe. As in, transcending the human condition to become something more is pretty much a major point of the game, and kind of the idea behind the Ubermensch. The idea of the Ubermensch also posits that the idea of God is meaningless and holds no value in current society - from a Mage perspective, that means that the Exarchs and serving them is bad. Which, it is. Wisdom isn't a code of conduct given from on high - its a personal understanding how to use your magic without it spiraling out of control.<br /> <br /> However, where I veer away from mages is the idea that the ubermensch is the result of genetic manipulation across generations, while mage is more about using magic to artificially evolve individuals. Genetics plays no part in mage transcendance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Genetics and artificial selection don't have anything to do with the idea of the ubermensch, at least not in any Nietzschean conception. Later commentators and embellishers either added or read eugenics into it, but at its core it is a wholly philosophical phenomenon. This would seem to dovetail well with Mages but honestly NWoD Mages still don't really fit the bill, as the Truth and the Supernal are still external value sets rather than internal. OWoD Mage on the other hand is all about that. The cultivation of the personal will and spirit to overcome the boundaries of Consensus, substituting your own reality in its place where you are the sole determinant of its boundaries and definitions, is pretty much what old school Ascension <i>is</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:57:57-07:00","id":899993,"title":"","content":"I read some of Nietzche's comments, which included things about mothers' greatest acomplishments including bearing great children. So, yeah. I disagree that its entirely on later people, but Nietzche himself that started that trend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T07:03:35-07:00","id":899996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899798#post899798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what \u00fcbermensch are. \u00fcbermensch are people who follow only their own code, who create their own value, uninfluenced by anyone or anything else. He isn't a creator of values for others to follow. He isn't a master imposing his will upon others.<br /> <br /> Demons can't be \u00fcbermensch, they know god exist, they define their entire existence by their opposition to god. They do not make their own values. Maybe reaching hell would make them \u00fcbermensch but they aren't yet.<br /> Beast cannot be \u00fcbermensch, they are slave to a parasitic astral monster.<br /> Changelings cannot be \u00fcbermensch. Their entire existence lies upon making pacts and stories, using these tools to impose rules and obey said rules on the universe and others. An \u00fcbermensch would follow his own rules.<br /> Sin eater cannot be Ubermensch, they too follow the rules of a symbiotic entity much like beasts do.<br /> Hunters could be \u00dcbermensch, in fact, they are the closest to the \u00fcbermensch, hunters make their own rules, set their own purpose. As long as they do not join a conspiracy, then they stop being \u00fcbermensch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagreement here.<br /> <br /> Only some Demon's define themselves entirely by their position relative to God(-Machine): Integrators and Saboteurs. And Saboteurs can easily want to do things their own way once the Machine is out of the picture. While all Demon's factor the external factor of the God-Machine into their lives, that's like saying you factor in things like Physics into your life. Aside from that, they <i>entirely</i> define their own values - Cover is how well hidden you are, no how well you abide by any code.<br /> <br /> Beasts Incarnate transcend that by <i>becoming </i>the monster they want to be. Entirely Ubermensch.<br /> <br /> Changelings too can define their own stories. The &quot;pacts and stories&quot; they rely on <i>are</i> their physics. Unless you are restricting Ubermensch to those who can warp reality to their whims, Changelings have nothing to disqualify them.<br /> <br /> A Sin-Eater's Synergy is the accord between them and their partner - which they agreed to. Within that, they can define value for themselves however they wish. The &quot;rules&quot; of the Geist are barely that.<br /> <br /> Hunters obey the same social rules everyone else does - because they are as mortal as everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:29:19-07:00","id":900053,"title":"","content":"Incarnate Beasts also tie themselves to a monstruous narrative that acts as the lynchpin of their power, defining themselves by the monomyth even if on different terms than everyone else (not that those terms are unimpeachable either). So they don't fit Elderand's prerequisites for being ubermensch, even if his reasoning on Beasts failing to fit the criteria is incorrect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:41:41-07:00","id":900074,"title":"","content":"Demons can't be ubermensch. They can make their own value and make their own way all they want it won't make them Ubermensch. The Ubermensch isn't just making your own values it's doing so because there is no god to give you other values. Nothing higher than the self.<br /> <br /> If god exist and you make your own value, you're not an Ubermensch, you're an heretic.<br /> <br /> And even then, that's not the only difference for demons. They don't actually make their own way, every single demon define itself by his relationship to the god machine, not just saboteur or integrator. Every single one of them has to tailor his existence to escape notice from the god machine, they can't just ignore it and do what they want.<br /> <br /> Changeling are the same, it's not just about pact and contract it's about the fact they define their entire existence by the true fae. <br /> <br /> And I don't agree the monster in beast is actually their true self, it's demonstrably not. It's not just a hunger or digestive system, it's a semi independent being that will do what it wants and roam free to cause fear all on its own if the person its attached to doesn't feed it. I do agree that integrating it does give them a chnace toward ubermensch status.<br /> <br /> As for sin eater. Synergy. The simple existence of Synergy proves one cannot be a sin eater and an ubermensch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:49:57-07:00","id":900086,"title":"","content":"If regular Mages can't be Ubermensch, what about Archmages? They are still part of groups with rules (Ententes), but their plans for Ascension are very personal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T09:23:03-07:00","id":900124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=900053#post900053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incarnate Beasts also tie themselves to a monstruous narrative that acts as the lynchpin of their power, defining themselves by the monomyth even if on different terms than everyone else (not that those terms are unimpeachable either). So they don't fit Elderand's prerequisites for being ubermensch, even if his reasoning on Beasts failing to fit the criteria is incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually reject the Monomyth in favor of one <i>of their own choosing</i>. Are they still bound by a myth? Yes, but it is one they defined themselves which is fully in keeping with the ubermench goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T09:30:00-07:00","id":900127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=900074#post900074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons can't be ubermensch. They can make their own value and make their own way all they want it won't make them Ubermensch. The Ubermensch isn't just making your own values it's doing so because there is no god to give you other values. Nothing higher than the self.<br /> <br /> If god exist and you make your own value, you're not an Ubermensch, you're an heretic.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the God-Machine has &quot;God&quot; in the name, would Nietzsche call it one for the purpose of his philosophy? His idea of God seems to imply the existence of an objective Value, and the God-Machine is an amoral entity. Like the Internet.<br /> <br /> Another question, where do the \u00dcbermensch get their rules from? At some point of their development as a person they must have internalized some external values. They could have accepted an entire philosophy wholesale, or synthesized it from multiple beliefs. Either way, nothing develops in a void. When a Werewolf embraces the laws of Luna to the point they shape their life around it and they'd sooner kill themselves or Luna herself than break them, I think the word \u00dcbermensch is appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T09:35:25-07:00","id":900129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=900074#post900074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons can't be ubermensch. They can make their own value and make their own way all they want it won't make them Ubermensch. The Ubermensch isn't just making your own values it's doing so because there is no god to give you other values. Nothing higher than the self.<br /> <br /> If god exist and you make your own value, you're not an Ubermensch, you're an heretic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then by your definition, Ubermensch are impossible. The God-Machine exists. Luna exists. Physical Laws exist. Any proposed Ubermensch would still be subject to laws (natural or logical), thus impossible. Maybe something in the Abyss?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=900074#post900074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even then, that's not the only difference for demons. They don't actually make their own way, every single demon define itself by his relationship to the god machine, not just saboteur or integrator. Every single one of them has to tailor his existence to escape notice from the god machine, they can't just ignore it and do what they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They only need to factor the God-Machine into their decisions in so much as avoiding a threat. Unless you are defining Ubermensch as &quot;no stronger force exists&quot;, which is impossible, that doesn't disqualify them. &quot;They can't just ignore it and do what they want&quot;. The same can be said about gravity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=900074#post900074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling are the same, it's not just about pact and contract it's about the fact they define their entire existence by the true fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Demons, they only need to interface with the True Fae in regards to something that posses a threat. Henceforth, they can define their own selves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=900074#post900074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't agree the monster in beast is actually their true self, it's demonstrably not. It's not just a hunger or digestive system, it's a semi independent being that will do what it wants and roam free to cause fear all on its own if the person its attached to doesn't feed it. I do agree that integrating it does give them a chnace toward ubermensch status.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can liken it to instincts, which can force you to do things you don't want. So are Ubermensch restricted to Transhumanists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T09:35:53-07:00","id":900132,"title":"","content":"&quot;You come here, spouting ideas about a concept you hardly understand, expecting for whatever misguided reason you might have that others will accept your opinion as the objective truth and conform to your limited vision of reality.<br /> <br /> Well, I say <i>no more</i>. I see no reason why I should <b>care</b> in the slightest about your pitiful dreams of a world constrained by your unsatisfactory and arbitrary notions of 'humanity'.<br /> <br /> You come here, seeking my imprisonment, telling me I am no longer a human, as if saying that somehow absolves you of your ignorance. I am a man, but also something more. I REFUSE a universe, where humanity is something only the weak somehow have the right to keep and that the currents of Power and Will shall take away in an instant.<br /> <br /> I cannot be caged. I cannot be controlled. Understand this as you die, ever pathetic, ever fools!&quot;<br /> <br /> [/self-demonstrating example]<br /> <br /> <br /> Bonus points for recognizing the reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T09:38:32-07:00","id":900136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=900132#post900132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot be caged. I cannot be controlled. Understand this as you die, ever pathetic, ever fools!&quot;<br /> <br /> Bonus points for recognizing the reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last one's Irenicus (as far as I am aware). The rest, I'm not sure, but sounds like something one of the Draculas from Castlevania would easily say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T09:39:52-07:00","id":900137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=900136#post900136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last one's Irenicus (as far as I am aware). The rest, I'm not sure, but sounds like something one of the Draculas from Castlevania would easily say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made the first part up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:14:26-07:00","id":900196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899798#post899798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what \u00fcbermensch are. \u00fcbermensch are people who follow only their own code, who create their own value, uninfluenced by anyone or anything else. He isn't a creator of values for others to follow. He isn't a master imposing his will upon others.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Rand, not Neitzsche.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:42:48-07:00","id":901416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=899846#post899846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not my criteria, it's the criteria laid out Nietzsche. And it's not about not having connections to anything, it's about only following your own moral code and rules. Not having your will subordinate to anything or anyone else. It's about being yourself without needing to belong to anything else.<br /> <br /> The \u00fcbermensch is impossible in the world of darkness not because there are connection but because there are gods, there are moral/ethical principles derived from on high.</div> </div> </div> </div> Everyone follows some sort of rules, if only thosecof physics, but even societal. Even criminals have respect some of a societies laws.<br /> <br /> So there can't be an absolute Overman (I think this is the english translation?), but there can be someone who is a relative Overman.<br /> <br /> Just a weird thought but what about a claimed whose goetic half is the idea of the Overman itself.<br /> <br /> Or a Prime could summon the platonic form of the Overman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T00:20:49-07:00","id":901837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899437-which-splats-are-the-best-for-playing-an-\u00fcbermensch?p=901416#post901416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone follows some sort of rules, if only thosecof physics, but even societal. Even criminals have respect some of a societies laws.<br /> <br /> So there can't be an absolute Overman (I think this is the english translation?), but there can be someone who is a relative Overman.<br /> <br /> Just a weird thought but what about a claimed whose goetic half is the idea of the Overman itself.<br /> <br /> Or a Prime could summon the platonic form of the Overman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uber in this sense is more above than over. In this context it is in referance to hierarchy. The Uber is saying they are above the common man, better than the common man. This is where \u00dcbermensch being perfection of the human form comes from in my understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:38:40-07:00","id":902182,"title":"","content":"Okay, so Integrity and its equivalent traits for each splat set a precedent of rules that PCs are supposed to follow. I don't think this thread will move unless we settle for a relative value of \u00dcbermensch.<br /> <br /> We can hypothesize ways for PCs to abandon the need for Integrity traits, but the canon methods for that (e.g. changelings becoming True Fae at Wyrd 10 and Clarity 0) distance them from our world, be it physically and/or mentally. Aren't \u00dcbermenschen supposed to embrace this world as it is and not run away from its challenges?<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, since Legacy Attainments don't risk Wisdom loss in 2ED, and the Mastigos are all about confronting your flaws and self-determination, a Legacy associated with that Path might be the closest we can get to an Over-Man in the strictest sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T20:06:19-07:00","id":903231,"title":"","content":"You all have a limited grasp on the superman concept of neitzsche. EVERYONE can attain or strive to attain the superman. The first thing one must understand is the 3 stages before one can even begin to transform into the superman. First is the camel, the beast of burden performing everyones will. Next you become the lion, after you transcend into your own power and slaughter the dragon with golden scales known only as &quot;thou shalt&quot; (Nietzsche wasn't a fan of christianity, rather referring to priests as the preachers of death in the book &quot;thus spoke zutharusta&quot;). Only after you have slain &quot;thou shalt&quot; can you become a child again, as you are now able to look at the world with new eyes and question everything on your own. Once you rise above that, through a superior set of morals and living can you become the superman. You become the superman through suffering and hard work. One should never take the easy path in life as that only produces the last man. <br /> <br /> By this token Lycoan from forsaken's hunting grounds may fit. He has transcended the simple morality of the forsaken society and has quite literally risen to god status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}